<div id="lstnumberx134" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx134.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">    </span><span id="lstnumberx134.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#B30000;">’True<span id="lstnumberx134.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Error<span id="lstnumberx134.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Rate’</span><span id="lstnumberx134.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">:</span><span id="lstnumberx134.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx134.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">product_totals</span><span id="lstnumberx134.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><span id="lstnumberx134.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#B30000;">’true_error_rate’</span><span id="lstnumberx134.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">],</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx135" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx135.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">    </span><span id="lstnumberx135.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#B30000;">’DP<span id="lstnumberx135.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Error<span id="lstnumberx135.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Rate’</span><span id="lstnumberx135.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">:</span><span id="lstnumberx135.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx135.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">dp_error_series</span><span id="lstnumberx135.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">,</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx136" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx136.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">    </span><span id="lstnumberx136.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#B30000;">’Z-Score’</span><span id="lstnumberx136.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">:</span><span id="lstnumberx136.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx136.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">z_scores</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx137" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx137.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">})</span>
</div>
</div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>. </span><span id="A4.F7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">LLM-generated Python code for computing user-level differentially private z-scores. We used this program for the error-identification study.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Z-score:</span> The following (see Figure <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix D Programs Used in the Error Identification Study ‣ DPCheatSheet: Using Worked and Erroneous LLM-usage Examples to Scaffold Differential Privacy Implementation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) presents a Python program to compute the z-score of the error rates of each product type using user-level pure differential privacy with <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>. (The error rates are computed by dividing the number of error events by the total number of events.) However, the implementation is incorrect. Please point out all the errors and briefly explain why they are incorrect.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Errors are: (1) Unprivatized data-dependent hyperparameters and (2) Overly noisy results.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Screenshots of the Interactive LLM-Driven DP Programming Interface</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See Figure <a href="#A5.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Appendix E Screenshots of the Interactive LLM-Driven DP Programming Interface ‣ DPCheatSheet: Using Worked and Erroneous LLM-usage Examples to Scaffold Differential Privacy Implementation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, <a href="#A5.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ Appendix E Screenshots of the Interactive LLM-Driven DP Programming Interface ‣ DPCheatSheet: Using Worked and Erroneous LLM-usage Examples to Scaffold Differential Privacy Implementation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, and <a href="#A5.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix E Screenshots of the Interactive LLM-Driven DP Programming Interface ‣ DPCheatSheet: Using Worked and Erroneous LLM-usage Examples to Scaffold Differential Privacy Implementation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12590v1/figures/GUI_req.png" id="A5.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/115;" width="215" height="115" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>. </span><span id="A5.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">In our initial interactive LLM-driven DP programming interface, users first upload a dataset, specify the query and configure differential privacy parameters.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12590v1/figures/GUI_code.png" id="A5.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:215/175;" width="215" height="175" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>. </span><span id="A5.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Then, the LLM-powered backbone generates Python code to compute DP solution for the specified query.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12590v1/figures/GUI_explanation.png" id="A5.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:238/204;" width="238" height="204" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>. </span><span id="A5.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Alongside the program, the LLM also generates a computational graph and explanation to help users understand the code.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
